// Title: Chromium Browser Instance Executed With Custom Extension
// Sigma ID: 88d6e60c-759d-4ac1-a447-c0f1466c2d21
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Aedan Russell, frack113, X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-19 | Modified: 2023-11-28
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1176.001
// Description: Detects a Chromium based browser process with the 'load-extension' flag to start a instance with
//   a custom extension
// False positives:
//   - Usage of Chrome Extensions in testing tools such as BurpSuite will trigger this alert
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/chromeloader/
//   - https://emkc.org/s/RJjuLa
//   - https://www.mandiant.com/resources/blog/lnk-between-browsers
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_browsers_chromium_load_extension.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\brave.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\chrome.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\msedge.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\opera.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\vivaldi.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "--load-extension="
